It's pretty stable, actually, I've never seen Slash'EM crash. Haven't
played a whole lot, but I don't see other people complaining either.

I would say that Slash'EM is a worthy successor if you'd like to play a
game that is like Vanilla NetHack but with a whole lot of new items,
monsters, and areas to play with. It also opens up some additional 
strategies (dopplegangers and class abilities come to mind) but they're
not things you need to win or enjoy the game. You can use more or less
the same strategies and come out ahead.

SporkHack, in contrast, doesn't have a whole lot of new items, monsters,
or areas (though it does have some). Instead it changes the overall game
balance so you need to devise new strategies and alter old strategies
to win; Slash'EM changes the things you need to make decisions about
and SporkHack changes the right decisions. I expect there are people
who would find either more interesting.

